            <ArticleTitle>Neonatal Gallstones Serendipitously Discovered by Point-of-Care Ultrasound in the Pediatric Emergency Department.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>734-735</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cholelithiasis in children was once thought to be uncommon, but the prevalence has increased in recent years. We present a case of a 3-month-old infant brought to the pediatric emergency department for vomiting and increased fussiness. A point-of-care ultrasound was performed to rule out pyloric stenosis but revealed multiple stones within the gallbladder. Ultrasound findings and a review of technique for ultrasound of the gallbladder are presented.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
